    {
      "_id": "dfZxyxdyW50Tcolf",
      "name": "Prices, Rooms & Stabling",
      "type": "text",
      "title": {
        "show": true,
        "level": 1
      },
      "image": {},
      "text": {
        "content": "<h2>Food &amp; drink</h2><table style=\"width:100%\"><thead><tr><th>Dish</th><th>Price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Simple vegetable stew</td><td>5 cc</td></tr><tr><td>Meat stew</td><td>10 cc</td></tr><tr><td>Meat cut and turnips</td><td>30 cc</td></tr><tr><td>Good meal (not slum)</td><td>50 cc</td></tr><tr><td>Luxury meal (not slum/poor)</td><td>10 sc</td></tr><tr><td>Banquet</td><td>20 sc</td></tr><tr><td>Beer (tankard)</td><td>2 cc</td></tr><tr><td>Mead (tankard)</td><td>2 cc</td></tr><tr><td>Cider (mug)</td><td>1 cc</td></tr><tr><td>Wine (mug)</td><td>3 cc</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Lodging (per night)</h2><table style=\"width:100%\"><thead><tr><th>Room</th><th>Price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dormitory</td><td>3 sc</td></tr><tr><td>Double room</td><td>5 sc</td></tr><tr><td>Single room</td><td>7 sc</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Stabling (per day)</h2><table style=\"width:100%\"><thead><tr><th>Animal</th><th>Price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Donkey/Mule</td><td>7 cc</td></tr><tr><td>Pony</td><td>6 cc</td></tr><tr><td>Light + medium horse</td><td>10 cc</td></tr><tr><td>Large horse</td><td>15 cc</td></tr><tr><td>Ox</td><td>9 cc</td></tr><tr><td>Elephant (not allowed in cities)</td><td>10 sc</td></tr><tr><td>Legendary animal (hippogriff, pegasus, etc.)</td><td>5 sc</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Entertainment</h2><p>Characters throw coins to the entertainers as payment. If a character owns less than 30 cc, they don't need to pay.</p><table style=\"width:100%\"><thead><tr><th>Entertainer</th><th>Payment</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Musician</td><td>1d6 cc</td></tr><tr><td>Dancing girls (male characters)</td><td>1d10 cc</td></tr><tr><td>Dancing girls (female characters)</td><td>1d3−1 cc</td></tr><tr><td>Jester</td><td>1d8 cc</td></tr></tbody></table><p><em>Source: Magi-regelboken (Magic Rulebook) p.48. Four types of inns: fine, normal, poor, and slum. An inn with no lodging is called a tavern.</em></p>",
